 # Forward Difference Gradient
 
-Also called: Forward Difference Method, Simple Forward Differencing Gradient, Intermediate Difference Gradient
+Also called: Forward Difference Method, Simple Forward Differencing Gradient
 
 ## Overview
-The Forward Difference Gradient estimates the spatial derivative of a scalar volume field at a voxel by comparing the value at the current voxel to the value at the immediately adjacent neighbor in the positive direction along each axis [S1, unofficial][S2][S3, unofficial]. It solves the problem of computing surface normals for lighting models in volume rendering using minimal computational resources [S5, unofficial]. Unlike the Central Difference method, which averages neighbors from both sides, the Forward Difference method is asymmetric and detects high-frequency details that may be smoothed out by central differencing, though it introduces anisotropy and orientation dependence [S4, unofficial].
